# Tuning applied to IDENTITY=own only.
#
# Appended to arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig right before the build generates
# its .config, so these are the last word on each symbol. NOT applied to `repro`,
# which has to stay an exact copy of the phone's kernel.
#
# Every symbol here is also what scripts/20-verify.sh is allowed to forgive, by
# construction: it reads this file and accepts exactly these symbols. A diff
# outside this list still fails the build.
#
# One entry per reason. If a knob cannot say why it is here, it does not belong.
# A knob whose premise turned out to be wrong gets deleted, not kept "just in
# case" -- see zram below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. KernelAddressSanitizer is off.
#
# The phone's config has CONFIG_KASAN=y with CONFIG_KASAN_HW_TAGS=y, i.e. memory
# tagging instrumentation active in a daily driver. It is a debugging feature:
# CPU cost on every allocation, memory cost for tags and redzones, and it buys
# nothing on a phone that is not being fuzzed.
#
# This does not touch CFI, pointer authentication or BTI: those stay.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_KASAN is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Debug symbols are not built.
#
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO with DWARF4 is ~1 GB of vmlinux nobody ships. It does not
# change the Image at all, only build time and artifact size. Turning it off is
# free.
#
# The two lines after it are not settings: they are the symbols that stop
# existing once DEBUG_INFO is off. They are listed so this file is a complete
# record of what the build changes. "The config dropped an option because its
# parent went away" is still a change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO is not set
# CONFIG_GDB_SCRIPTS is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_EFI is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Removed: zram.
#
# The first version of this file enabled CONFIG_ZRAM, CONFIG_ZSMALLOC and
# CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZO on the theory that the kernel had no swap, so Android was
# killing apps instead of compressing cold pages.
#
# That theory was wrong, and the device said so:
#
#   zram0 already in use: 8388604 kB   SwapTotal: 8388604 kB
#   algorithms: lzo [lzo-rle] lz4 zstd
#
# Your ROM already brings zram up with 8 GB and lzo-rle. The kernel config does
# not show it because the ROM loads zram as a vendor module from vendor_dlkm, and
# built-in config cannot see vendor modules at all.
#
# Enabling it here as well would duplicate a driver the vendor also loads, for
# exactly zero benefit. Deleted.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
